    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōpōnĭus</span></b> ,
		a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a plebeian family at Rome</i>, e. g. the two
			brothers, T. and C. Coponii, <i><span class="en">Cic. Cael.
				10, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Balb. 23, 53</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōpōnĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to Coponius</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				12, 31, 2</span></i>.</div>
